#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Candidate Bridge 1.9: VERIFY / TEST_PR / derived DEPLOY plans / CANARY / ROLLBACK,
plus a read-only CONTROL_PLANE_HEALTH probe.

The DEPLOY plan is derived, not registered.  Until this revision the plan bundle was
written by an operator, which made "a human maintains the deployment plan" a necessary
step of every deployment -- and the scope contract names exactly that as a V1 failure
rather than an operating rule.  A DEPLOY Request is now the five common fields, exactly
like a CANARY Request: it names an action and an environment and steers nothing.  On
arrival the Bridge joins the facts it already holds -- the candidate admission record,
the root-owned live baseline, the signed TEST_PR of that candidate, and the canary and
preflight Tasks it published and signed itself -- derives the plan, validates it in
memory against the gate, registers it, and reads it back before signing the Task.  The
approval is the Request itself: the identity GitHub reports for its author, the moment
GitHub reports it was created, and the digest of its canonical content.

The canary action takes nothing from the Request either.  A CANARY Request is the five
common fields; the candidate image, its sealed package and the image the canary expects
to be current are read from a root-owned authority file, so no caller can steer what the
canary executes.  CANARY is deliberately *not* gated by the deployment authorisation:
the canary is the evidence a deployment plan must cite before that plan can exist, so the
authorisation for a deployment cannot be a precondition for producing it.  Installing this
revision authorises no deployment at all.

A ROLLBACK Request is likewise the five common fields, and what it undoes is not named by
the caller either: the Bridge takes the newest deployment it published whose signed
Evidence reports DEPLOY_OK -- its own record of its own act -- and authorises exactly that
pair.  The host decides whether the rollback is still meaningful, by re-hashing the
deployment's record and re-reading the eight containers immediately before it acts, so a
caller cannot choose a target and a stale authorisation cannot cause one.  ROLLBACK is
gated by the same `deployment_authorization` declaration as DEPLOY, so the emergency stop
that silences deployments silences rollbacks with them, and the read-only probes stay up.

The health action is kept apart from the rest: it is deliberately not a member of the
same family.

* It carries no parameters. Its Request schema is the five common fields and nothing
  else, so there is no field a caller could use to steer an execution; the parameter
  block on the Task is a fixed constant rather than anything read out of the Request.
* It is signed with the existing task identity, because what is signed is a Task
  identity and not an approval. It grants no execution, takes no part in the DEPLOY
  arm, the approved plan or the release budget, and does not touch the deployment
  authorisation.
* It exists for one purpose: to let the HK agent publish fresh signed liveness
  Evidence, so `hk_agent_online` can be answered from a signature instead of from a
  reachability guess.

A DEPLOY Request used to carry a `plan_id` naming a plan a human had written.  It no
longer carries one -- not because the field moved, but because there is nothing left for
it to select: the plan name is a function of the candidate and of the canary run that
witnessed the host, so a caller-chosen name would be a caller-chosen deployment.

There is no deploy switch any more either.  Until this revision the Bridge refused every
DEPLOY Request until an operator had set `deployment_requests_enabled` to true in the
root-owned channel configuration -- a standing authorisation, granted before the thing it
authorised existed.  That inverted the order of the world: the authority V1 defines is the
authenticated DEPLOY Request itself (`docs/project/CC_V1_SCOPE_20260916.md`), so a switch
that has to be flipped first makes a human server operation a necessary step of every
deployment, which that document names as V1 not being delivered.  The configuration now
declares only *how* deployments are authorised, and every DEPLOY Request must still come
from an authorised GitHub identity, cite a fresh canary and preflight, and name the exact
candidate.  Setting the mode to anything but `request` refuses DEPLOY Requests and nothing
else, so it still works as an emergency stop.

Dispatch is explicit and fail-closed. An action that is not named in
`derive_formal_task` is refused; it can never fall through into VERIFY, TEST_PR,
DEPLOY or ROLLBACK, and before this revision an unnamed action silently became a
VERIFY. Nothing that the other three actions do or are allowed to do is changed.

A DEPLOY and a ROLLBACK are each followed by a VERIFY this Bridge publishes by itself.
Both actions end with the host in a state that a signed Evidence describes, and the
question that comes next -- is Hong Kong really in that state? -- used to need an
operator to send a second VERIFY by hand.  That made "the deployment succeeded" and "the
rollback succeeded" depend on somebody remembering to look, which is the gap PR #179
recorded against this channel.  The Bridge now reads the Evidence of the action it
published, checks both signatures, takes the image out of the verified bytes, signs a
VERIFY Task bound to that action, and publishes it.

That is additive and it grants nothing new.  VERIFY is read-only; the trigger is a signed
pair this Bridge published rather than a Request; the image is never supplied by anyone;
and the deployment authorisation still governs DEPLOY and ROLLBACK alone, so those two
actions keep exactly the authority they had.  What the VERIFY is for is the Control State:
`command-center-state-v1` reads the newest VERIFY Evidence as the image that was current,
so an automatic one is what makes `live_proven_image` track the host without a human.
"""
import argparse, datetime as dt, fcntl, hashlib, json, os, pathlib, re, secrets, subprocess, sys, tempfile
from cryptography.hazmat.primitives import serialization
import go_deploy_request as deploy_gate
import plan_derivation

REPO = "git@github.com:chenzhenxi1-sudo/go-control-tasks.git"
REQUEST_RE = re.compile(r"^requests/[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,127}\.json$")
REQUEST_ID_RE = re.compile(r"^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{2,79}$")
ALLOWED = {"schema_version", "request_id", "action_id", "environment", "requested_at"}
POLICY = {"schema_version": "1", "action_id": "HK_STAGING_VERIFY", "environment": "HK-STAGING-01", "max_bytes": 4096, "max_age_seconds": 900}
BASELINE_CONFIG = "/etc/go-command-center/boss-request-verify-baseline-v1.json"
CANARY_BASELINE_CONFIG = "/etc/go-command-center/boss-request-canary-baseline-v1.json"
TEST_ACTION = "HK_STAGING_TEST_PR"
TEST_ALLOWED = ALLOWED | {"pr_number"}
CANARY_ACTION = "HK_STAGING_CANARY"
HEALTH_ACTION = "CONTROL_PLANE_HEALTH"
# The one and only parameter block a health Task may carry. It is a constant, not
# anything derived from the Request: the Request for this action is the five common
# fields, so it has no field that could contribute here even if someone tried.
HEALTH_PARAMETERS = {}
# The channel action contract, in full. The config has always been checked against an
# exact list rather than a membership test; health is a member of that contract, not a
# free-form toggle, so removing it takes a new Bridge revision rather than an edit to a
# root-owned config file. ROLLBACK sits next to DEPLOY because it is the same kind of
# act: it mutates the eight business services, it is authorised by an authenticated
# Request, and it is silenced by the same declaration.
CHANNEL_ACTIONS = [POLICY["action_id"], TEST_ACTION, deploy_gate.ACTION,
                   deploy_gate.ROLLBACK_ACTION, CANARY_ACTION, HEALTH_ACTION]
# How a deployment is authorised. There is no standing switch to turn on: the authority is
# the authenticated DEPLOY Request the authorised identity opened, and the Command Center
# derives a one-time authorisation from it per request. This field declares that mode and
# carries no authority of its own -- setting it to `request` grants nothing, because a
# deployment still needs an authorised Request, a fresh canary, a fresh preflight and the
# exact candidate. Any other value refuses every DEPLOY Request and nothing else.
AUTHORIZATION_MODE = "request"
GO_REPOSITORY = "git@github.com:yuguangzhi3836-glitch/GO.git"
PR_RESOLVER_KEY = "/etc/go-command-center/keys/github-go-pr-resolver"
# Both already exist and are read-only: the evidence reader was provisioned for the
# evidence repository, and the GO resolver for the candidate pointer. Neither is new
# authority, and neither can write anything.
EVIDENCE_REPO = "git@github.com:chenzhenxi1-sudo/go-control-evidence.git"
EVIDENCE_READER_KEY = "/etc/go-command-center/keys/github-evidence-reader"
EVIDENCE_NAME_RE = re.compile(r"^evidence/[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,127}-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,128}\.json$")
COMMIT_SHA_RE = re.compile(r"^[0-9a-f]{40}$")
PR_NUMBER_RE = re.compile(r"^[1-9][0-9]{0,8}$")
# A branch name that may be handed to git as an argument.  It is stated by the remote,
# so it is validated before use: a name beginning with `-` would otherwise be read as
# an option rather than as a ref.
DEFAULT_BRANCH_RE = re.compile(r"^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._/-]{0,127}$")

Reject = deploy_gate.Reject

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# The automatic post-action VERIFY
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Pinned from the executor that produces them: `hk-staging/source/executor/runtime/
# rollback_runtime.py` returns exactly these seven names on success.  A VERIFY derived
# from a rollback whose own gates did not all pass would be derived from a state the
# executor never claimed, so they are asserted rather than the looser "every value is
# PASS" -- the rollback Evidence carries record ids and the source task id beside the
# gates, and the loose rule would refuse every real rollback.
ROLLBACK_RESULT_GATES = ("rollback_source", "lineage", "target_derivation", "fresh_drift",
                         "rollback_record", "fixed_scope", "postcheck")
POST_VERIFY_ACTIONS = (deploy_gate.ACTION, deploy_gate.ROLLBACK_ACTION)
POST_VERIFY_RESULT = {deploy_gate.ACTION: "DEPLOY_OK",
                      deploy_gate.ROLLBACK_ACTION: "ROLLBACK_OK"}
POST_VERIFY_GATES = {deploy_gate.ACTION: deploy_gate.DEPLOY_GATES,
                     deploy_gate.ROLLBACK_ACTION: ROLLBACK_RESULT_GATES}
# Beside the ledger, not inside it.  The ledger's `requests` mapping is read by other
# units to decide which deployment a rollback undoes and which VERIFY is a deployment's
# preflight; a synthesised Task in there would be offered to both, and a post-action
# VERIFY must never be mistaken for either.
POST_VERIFY_STORE = "post-action-verifies.json"
# The Evidence has to still describe the host.  An action that finished longer ago than
# this has a successor, and publishing a VERIFY that asserts the older state would
# manufacture a failure instead of reporting one.
POST_VERIFY_MAX_AGE = dt.timedelta(seconds=1800)
POST_VERIFY_TASK_LIFE = dt.timedelta(minutes=20)
IMAGE_ID = re.compile(r"^sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}$")

def canonical(value): return json.dumps(value, sort_keys=True, separators=(",", ":"), ensure_ascii=False).encode()
def now(): return dt.datetime.now(dt.timezone.utc)
def iso(value): return value.isoformat().replace("+00:00", "Z")
def parse_time(value):
    if not isinstance(value, str): raise Reject("requested_at_not_string")
    try: return dt.datetime.fromisoformat(value.replace("Z", "+00:00"))
    except ValueError as exc: raise Reject("invalid_requested_at") from exc

def validate_request(raw, at=None):
    if len(raw) > POLICY["max_bytes"]: raise Reject("request_oversized")
    try: request = deploy_gate.parse_json(raw)
    except (UnicodeDecodeError, json.JSONDecodeError) as exc: raise Reject("malformed_json") from exc
    if not isinstance(request, dict): raise Reject("schema_fields")
    action=request.get('action_id')
    if not isinstance(action,str): raise Reject('action')
    # DEPLOY carries the five common fields and nothing else.  A plan_id used to name a
    # plan a human had written; the plan is derived now, so a caller-chosen name would
    # only be a caller-chosen deployment.  A Request that still carries one is refused by
    # the exact-set comparison below rather than being read as if the field were ignored.
    fields = TEST_ALLOWED if action == TEST_ACTION else ALLOWED
    if set(request) != fields: raise Reject("schema_fields")
    if request["schema_version"] != POLICY["schema_version"]: raise Reject("schema_version")
    if not isinstance(request["request_id"], str) or not REQUEST_ID_RE.fullmatch(request["request_id"]): raise Reject("request_id")
    if request["action_id"] not in {POLICY["action_id"], TEST_ACTION, deploy_gate.ACTION, deploy_gate.ROLLBACK_ACTION, CANARY_ACTION, HEALTH_ACTION}: raise Reject("action")
    if request["environment"] != POLICY["environment"]: raise Reject("environment")
    when = parse_time(request["requested_at"])
    at = at or now()
    if when.tzinfo is None or when > at + dt.timedelta(seconds=60) or at - when > dt.timedelta(seconds=POLICY["max_age_seconds"]): raise Reject("stale_or_future_request")
    if request["action_id"] == TEST_ACTION and (not isinstance(request["pr_number"],str) or not PR_NUMBER_RE.fullmatch(request["pr_number"])): raise Reject("pr_number")
    return request

def load_baseline(path=BASELINE_CONFIG):
    value=json.loads(pathlib.Path(path).read_text())
    required={"version","environment","image_id","evidence_task_id","evidence_commit","evidence_path"}
    if set(value) != required or value["version"] != 1 or value["environment"] != POLICY["environment"]: raise Reject("invalid_authoritative_baseline")
    if not re.fullmatch(r"sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}",value["image_id"]): raise Reject("invalid_authoritative_baseline")
    if not all(isinstance(value[x],str) and value[x] for x in ("evidence_task_id","evidence_commit","evidence_path")): raise Reject("invalid_authoritative_baseline")
    return value
def load_canary_baseline(path=CANARY_BASELINE_CONFIG):
    if path==CANARY_BASELINE_CONFIG:
        try: active=deploy_gate.candidate_contract.active()
        except deploy_gate.candidate_contract.Reject as exc: raise Reject(str(exc)) from exc
        if active:
            record,contract=active
            return {"version":2,"environment":POLICY["environment"],"candidate_image_id":contract["candidate"]["image_id"],"candidate_package_sha256":contract["candidate"]["package_sha256"],"expected_current_image_id":contract["expected_current_image_id"],"candidate_contract_sha256":record["candidate_contract_sha256"]}
    """The root-owned binding a CANARY Request may not influence.

    A canary Task names a candidate image, that candidate's sealed package, and the
    image the canary expects to be current.  None of the three may come from a
    Request: the Request is an untrusted proposal and the canary is evidence, so the
    values come from this file, which the operator writes (root:root 0600) and the
    Bridge only reads.  A file that is missing, unreadable, malformed, incomplete,
    over-broad or off-environment is refused rather than defaulted -- and it is
    refused as a Reject, so the polling tick reports a rejection instead of dying.
    """
    try:
        value=json.loads(pathlib.Path(path).read_text())
    except (OSError, UnicodeDecodeError, json.JSONDecodeError) as exc:
        raise Reject("invalid_canary_authority") from exc
    required={"version","environment","candidate_image_id","candidate_package_sha256","expected_current_image_id"}
    if not isinstance(value,dict) or set(value) != required or value.get("version") != 1 or value.get("environment") != POLICY["environment"]:
        raise Reject("invalid_canary_authority")
    if not re.fullmatch(r"sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}",value["candidate_image_id"]): raise Reject("invalid_canary_authority")
    if not re.fullmatch(r"sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}",value["expected_current_image_id"]): raise Reject("invalid_canary_authority")
    if not re.fullmatch(r"[0-9a-f]{64}",value["candidate_package_sha256"]): raise Reject("invalid_canary_authority")
    return value

def derive(request, baseline, at=None):
    at = at or now(); stamp = at.strftime("%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ")
    # Seconds alone are insufficient for a persistent channel: two independent
    # PRs can be accepted in one poll.  The request-id digest makes task and
    # release identity deterministic per request without granting caller input
    # control over any deployment parameter.
    suffix=hashlib.sha256(request["request_id"].encode()).hexdigest()[:12]
    unique_stamp=stamp+"-"+suffix
    return {"schema_version":"1", "task_id":"go-boss-request-verify-" + unique_stamp,
      "nonce":secrets.token_urlsafe(24), "issued_at":iso(at), "expires_at":iso(at + dt.timedelta(minutes=15)),
      "authority":"GO-COMMAND-CENTER", "environment":POLICY["environment"], "action_id":POLICY["action_id"],
      "parameters":{"release_id":"boss-request-verify-" + unique_stamp, "candidate_image_id":baseline["image_id"], "expected_current_image_id":baseline["image_id"]}}

def derive_canary(request, baseline, at=None):
    """A candidate canary Task. It takes nothing at all from the Request.

    The Request schema for this action is the five common fields -- no image, no
    package, no service, no path, no env, no command, no plan, no pr_number -- so
    there is no caller-controlled field to pass through.  Every parameter is copied
    from the root-owned canary authority, which means two Requests against the same
    authority can differ only in identity and timing.

    The canary runs the candidate image in an isolated container (no network, read-only
    root, dropped capabilities) and asserts the pre-migration Alembic head.  It mutates
    no business runtime, which is why it does not need the deploy switch.
    """
    at = at or now(); stamp = at.strftime("%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ")
    suffix = hashlib.sha256(request["request_id"].encode()).hexdigest()[:12]
    unique_stamp = stamp + "-" + suffix
    return {"schema_version":"1", "task_id":"go-boss-request-canary-" + unique_stamp,
      "nonce":secrets.token_urlsafe(24), "issued_at":iso(at), "expires_at":iso(at + dt.timedelta(minutes=15)),
      "authority":"GO-COMMAND-CENTER", "environment":POLICY["environment"], "action_id":CANARY_ACTION,
      "parameters":{"release_id":"boss-request-canary-" + unique_stamp,
                    "candidate_image_id":baseline["candidate_image_id"],
                    "candidate_package_sha256":baseline["candidate_package_sha256"],
                    "expected_current_image_id":baseline["expected_current_image_id"],
                    **({"candidate_contract_sha256":baseline["candidate_contract_sha256"]} if "candidate_contract_sha256" in baseline else {})}}

def sign(task, key_path):
    key = serialization.load_pem_private_key(pathlib.Path(key_path).read_bytes(), password=None)
    signed = dict(task); signed["signature"] = key.sign(canonical(task)).hex(); return signed

def readonly_env(key_path):
    """A git environment that authenticates with one dedicated read-only Deploy Key."""
    env={"PATH":"/usr/bin:/bin","LC_ALL":"C","GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT":"0","GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM":"1","GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL":"/dev/null"}
    env["GIT_SSH_COMMAND"]="ssh -i %s -o IdentitiesOnly=yes -o BatchMode=yes -o StrictHostKeyChecking=yes" % key_path
    return env

def pr_resolver_env():
    """The GO resolver uses only its dedicated read-only Deploy Key."""
    return readonly_env(PR_RESOLVER_KEY)

def resolve_pr(number):
    if not isinstance(number,str) or not PR_NUMBER_RE.fullmatch(number): raise Reject("pr_number")
    ref="refs/pull/%s/head" % number
    try: lines=git(pr_resolver_env(),"ls-remote",GO_REPOSITORY,ref).stdout.splitlines()
    except (OSError,subprocess.SubprocessError) as exc: raise Reject("pr_resolution_unavailable") from exc
    if len(lines)!=1: raise Reject("pr_head_not_found")
    parts=lines[0].split("\t")
    if len(parts)!=2 or parts[1]!=ref or not COMMIT_SHA_RE.fullmatch(parts[0]): raise Reject("pr_head_invalid")
    return parts[0]

def remote_default_branch(env, repo):
    """The branch a reader gets by default -- asked of the remote, never assumed.

    The Bridge reads two remotes that do not agree on a name, and one of them does not
    carry `main` at all.  Hard-coding the branch here meant the evidence remote could
    never be read: its publication branch is whatever `git clone` checks out for the
    agent that writes it, and that agent's own contract leaves the branch untouched, so
    the name is a property of the remote rather than a constant of this program.  It is
    therefore resolved from the remote and validated before it is passed to git.
    """
    for line in git(env,"ls-remote","--symref",repo,"HEAD").stdout.splitlines():
        parts=line.split("\t")
        if len(parts)==2 and parts[1]=="HEAD" and parts[0].startswith("ref: refs/heads/"):
            name=parts[0][len("ref: refs/heads/"):]
            if DEFAULT_BRANCH_RE.fullmatch(name): return name
    raise Reject("readable_file_unavailable")

def read_repo_file(repo, key_path, path):
    """One file out of a read-only remote, by shallow filtered fetch.

    `--filter=blob:none` keeps the transfer to commits and trees, which is what makes
    this work at all against the GO repository: it carries more than a gigabyte of
    history, and a shallow fetch of it without the filter does not finish inside a poll
    tick.  The single blob this function is actually after is then fetched on demand by
    the `show` below.  No working tree is kept, and the branch is the remote's own
    default rather than a name guessed here.
    """
    work=pathlib.Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="go-cc-read-")); env=readonly_env(key_path)
    try:
        branch=remote_default_branch(env,repo)
        git(env,"init","-q",str(work)); git(env,"-C",str(work),"remote","add","origin",repo)
        git(env,"-C",str(work),"fetch","-q","--depth","1","--filter=blob:none","origin",branch)
        got=subprocess.run(["/usr/bin/git","-C",str(work),"show","FETCH_HEAD:"+path],
                           env=env,stdout=subprocess.PIPE,stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL)
        if got.returncode!=0: raise Reject("readable_file_unavailable")
        return got.stdout
    except (OSError,subprocess.SubprocessError) as exc:
        raise Reject("readable_file_unavailable") from exc
    finally: subprocess.run(["/usr/bin/rm","-rf",str(work)],check=True)

def read_admission():
    """The candidate admission record, as the GO repository publishes it."""
    try: active=deploy_gate.candidate_contract.active()
    except deploy_gate.candidate_contract.Reject as exc: raise Reject(str(exc)) from exc
    if active: return active[0]["admission"]
    return deploy_gate.parse_json(read_repo_file(
        GO_REPOSITORY, PR_RESOLVER_KEY, plan_derivation.ADMISSION_POINTER))

def read_evidence(task):
    """The signed Evidence of one published Task, addressed by the Task itself.

    The HK agent writes one file per execution named "<task_id>-<nonce>.json", so the
    Task the Bridge signed is what addresses its own result.  That is why the ledger
    holds no Evidence: the lookup key is already signed, and a substituted file cannot
    pass the gate, which re-verifies the signature and binds the content.
    """
    task_id=task.get("task_id"); nonce=task.get("nonce")
    if not isinstance(task_id,str) or not isinstance(nonce,str): raise Reject("evidence_unaddressed")
    name="evidence/%s-%s.json" % (task_id,nonce)
    if not EVIDENCE_NAME_RE.fullmatch(name): raise Reject("evidence_unaddressed")
    return deploy_gate.parse_json(read_repo_file(EVIDENCE_REPO, EVIDENCE_READER_KEY, name))

def derive_test_pr(request, at=None, resolver=resolve_pr):
    commit=resolver(request["pr_number"])
    if not COMMIT_SHA_RE.fullmatch(commit): raise Reject("pr_head_invalid")
    at=at or now(); suffix=hashlib.sha256(request["request_id"].encode()).hexdigest()[:12]
    return {"schema_version":"1","task_id":"go-boss-test-pr-%s-%s"%(request["pr_number"],suffix),"nonce":secrets.token_urlsafe(24),"issued_at":iso(at),"expires_at":iso(at+dt.timedelta(minutes=20)),"authority":"GO-COMMAND-CENTER","environment":POLICY["environment"],"action_id":TEST_ACTION,"parameters":{"builder_profile":"go-application-python-v1","source":{"repository":GO_REPOSITORY,"pr_number":request["pr_number"],"commit_sha":commit}}}

def derive_health(request, at=None):
    """A read-only liveness probe Task. It takes nothing at all from the Request.

    The Request schema for this action is the five common fields -- no image, no
    service, no path, no env, no command, no plan, no pr_number -- so there is no
    caller-controlled field to pass through. The parameter block is the module
    constant, copied rather than derived.
    """
    at = at or now(); suffix = hashlib.sha256(request["request_id"].encode()).hexdigest()[:12]
    return {"schema_version":"1", "task_id":"go-boss-health-"+at.strftime("%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ")+"-"+suffix,
      "nonce":secrets.token_urlsafe(24), "issued_at":iso(at), "expires_at":iso(at + dt.timedelta(minutes=15)),
      "authority":"GO-COMMAND-CENTER", "environment":POLICY["environment"],
      "action_id":HEALTH_ACTION, "parameters":dict(HEALTH_PARAMETERS)}

def derive_formal_task(request, at=None, resolver=resolve_pr):
    # Explicit dispatch, fail-closed. Every named action is bound to its own builder
    # and anything else is refused. The order matters for readability only; no branch
    # can hand a Request to another action's builder, and there is no fallthrough:
    # an unnamed action used to reach derive(), i.e. it silently became a VERIFY.
    action = request["action_id"]
    if action == HEALTH_ACTION: return derive_health(request, at)
    if action == TEST_ACTION: return derive_test_pr(request, at, resolver)
    if action == POLICY["action_id"]: return derive(request, load_baseline(), at)
    if action == CANARY_ACTION: return derive_canary(request, load_canary_baseline(), at)
    if action == deploy_gate.ACTION: raise Reject("deployment_context_required")
    if action == deploy_gate.ROLLBACK_ACTION: raise Reject("rollback_context_required")
    raise Reject("action_not_enabled_in_channel")

def derive_deployment(request,context,at=None):
    at=at or now(); suffix=secrets.token_hex(12)
    return {'schema_version':'1','task_id':'go-boss-deploy-'+suffix,'nonce':secrets.token_urlsafe(24),
      'issued_at':iso(at),'expires_at':iso(context['deadline']),'authority':'GO-COMMAND-CENTER',
      'environment':POLICY['environment'],'action_id':deploy_gate.ACTION,
      'parameters':{'release_id':'boss-deploy-'+suffix,**context['parameters']}}

def derive_rollback_task(request,context,at=None):
    """The ROLLBACK Task, from the derived context alone.

    It carries three parameters and no more, because the HK agent's own validator refuses
    any other name and any missing one: the release id this run and its Evidence are
    addressed by, the deployment to undo, and the authorisation id the Command Center
    derived.  There is no image, no service, no path, no command and no rollback target
    here, and there cannot be -- the executor reads those out of the source deployment's
    record, which it re-hashes itself.

    The Task id is the release id under the `go-` prefix every Bus task id carries, so one
    name addresses the run, the Task file and the Evidence file that reports it.
    """
    at = at or now(); release_id = context['parameters']['release_id']
    return {'schema_version':'1','task_id':'go-'+release_id,'nonce':secrets.token_urlsafe(24),
      'issued_at':iso(at),'expires_at':iso(context['deadline']),'authority':'GO-COMMAND-CENTER',
      'environment':POLICY['environment'],'action_id':deploy_gate.ROLLBACK_ACTION,
      'parameters':dict(context['parameters'])}

def check_deploy_pr(number,head):
    """Read PR metadata using a server-only, read-only request-repository token."""
    import urllib.request
    if not PR_NUMBER_RE.fullmatch(str(number)) or not COMMIT_SHA_RE.fullmatch(head): raise Reject('request_pr_identity')
    token=deploy_gate.read_secure('/etc/go-command-center/keys/github-requests-reader.token',4096).decode().strip()
    if not token or any(c.isspace() for c in token): raise Reject('request_reader_credential_invalid')
    class NoRedirect(urllib.request.HTTPRedirectHandler):
        def redirect_request(self,*args,**kwargs): raise Reject('request_api_redirect')
    request=urllib.request.Request('https://api.github.com/repos/chenzhenxi1-sudo/go-control-tasks/pulls/'+str(number),
        headers={'Authorization':'Bearer '+token,'Accept':'application/vnd.github+json','X-GitHub-Api-Version':'2022-11-28'})
    try:
        with urllib.request.build_opener(NoRedirect()).open(request,timeout=15) as response:
            raw=response.read(262145)
        if len(raw)>262144: raise Reject('request_metadata_oversized')
        value=deploy_gate.parse_json(raw)
    except Exception as exc: raise Reject('request_metadata_unavailable') from exc
    if (not isinstance(value,dict) or not all(isinstance(value.get(k),dict) and isinstance(value[k].get('repo'),dict) for k in ('head','base'))
        or value.get('state')!='open' or value.get('draft') is not False or value.get('merged') is not False
        or value.get('base',{}).get('ref')!='main' or value.get('base',{}).get('repo',{}).get('full_name')!='chenzhenxi1-sudo/go-control-tasks'
        or value.get('head',{}).get('repo',{}).get('full_name')!='chenzhenxi1-sudo/go-control-tasks'
        or value.get('head',{}).get('sha')!=head): raise Reject('request_pr_not_open_exact_head')
    # The approval authority is who GitHub says authored this pull request. The
    # reader token above reads GitHub's own answer, so an unauthorised author is
    # refused here and never reaches the plan.
    login=value.get('user',{}).get('login')
    if not isinstance(login,str) or login not in deploy_gate.APPROVAL_IDENTITIES:
        raise Reject('request_pr_author_not_authorised')
    # When the platform says the approval was given. This is a fact read from GitHub
    # rather than a timestamp an approver writes, which is what lets the approval window
    # stay exactly as strict as it was: the approval must still be younger than 15
    # minutes and later than both proofs.
    created=value.get('created_at')
    if not isinstance(created,str): raise Reject('request_pr_created_at_missing')
    try: moment=dt.datetime.fromisoformat(created.replace('Z','+00:00'))
    except ValueError as exc: raise Reject('request_pr_created_at_invalid') from exc
    if moment.tzinfo is None: raise Reject('request_pr_created_at_invalid')
    return value,login

class Ledger:
    def __init__(self, root): self.root = pathlib.Path(root); self.root.mkdir(mode=0o700, parents=True, exist_ok=True); self.path=self.root/"ledger.json"; self.lock=self.root/"ledger.lock"
    def transaction(self):
        handle=open(self.lock, "a+"); fcntl.flock(handle, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        try:
            data=json.loads(self.path.read_text()) if self.path.exists() else {"version":1,"requests":{}}
            yield data
            self.save(data)
        finally: fcntl.flock(handle, fcntl.LOCK_UN); handle.close()
    def save(self,data):
        temp=self.root/'ledger.tmp'
        fd=os.open(temp,os.O_WRONLY|os.O_CREAT|os.O_TRUNC|os.O_NOFOLLOW,0o600)
        with os.fdopen(fd,'wb') as stream:
            stream.write(canonical(data));stream.flush();os.fsync(stream.fileno())
        os.replace(temp,self.path)
        fd=os.open(self.root,os.O_RDONLY|os.O_DIRECTORY)
        try: os.fsync(fd)
        finally: os.close(fd)

def git(env, *argv, cwd=None): return subprocess.run(["/usr/bin/git", *argv], cwd=cwd, env=env, check=True, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.PIPE, text=True)

def ledger_records(ledger_root):
    """The durable ledger as it stands on disk right now, not a claim-time snapshot.

    The publish-time recheck needs to see what the ledger actually holds: another
    deployment published between the claim and the publication is exactly the thing that
    changes which deployment a rollback would undo, and the snapshot this process loaded
    when it took the claim cannot show it.  `Ledger.save` writes a temporary file and
    renames it over the target, so a reader never observes a partial ledger and needs no
    lock to read one.
    """
    try: return json.loads((pathlib.Path(ledger_root)/"ledger.json").read_text())["requests"]
    except (OSError,ValueError,TypeError,KeyError) as exc: raise Reject("ledger_unavailable") from exc
def ssh_env():
    env=os.environ.copy(); env["GIT_SSH_COMMAND"]="ssh -i /etc/go-command-center/keys/github-tasks-writer -o IdentitiesOnly=yes -o BatchMode=yes -o StrictHostKeyChecking=yes"; return env
def discover_heads():
    output=git(ssh_env(), "ls-remote", REPO, "refs/pull/*/head").stdout.splitlines(); heads={}
    for line in output:
        sha, ref=line.split("\t",1); number=ref.split("/")[2]; heads[number]=sha
    return heads
def request_path_from_changes(changes):
    """Accept only one added Request JSON file; every other PR diff is ignored."""
    if len(changes) != 1: return None
    parts=changes[0].split("\t")
    if len(parts) != 2 or parts[0] != "A" or not REQUEST_RE.fullmatch(parts[1]): return None
    return parts[1]
def read_pr(number, head):
    work=pathlib.Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="go-boss-request-")); env=ssh_env()
    try:
        git(env,"init","-q",str(work)); git(env,"-C",str(work),"remote","add","origin",REPO)
        git(env,"-C",str(work),"fetch","-q","--depth","128","origin","main:refs/bridge/main","refs/pull/%s/head:refs/bridge/head" % number)
        actual=git(env,"-C",str(work),"rev-parse","refs/bridge/head").stdout.strip()
        if actual != head or discover_heads().get(str(number)) != head: raise Reject("pr_head_changed")
        # Main may advance with unrelated formal Tasks after the Request fork.
        # Compare from the actual common ancestor; never misclassify them as PR deletions.
        base=git(env,'-C',str(work),'merge-base','refs/bridge/main','refs/bridge/head').stdout.strip()
        if not COMMIT_SHA_RE.fullmatch(base): raise Reject('request_merge_base_unavailable')
        changes=git(env,"-C",str(work),"diff","--name-status",base,'refs/bridge/head').stdout.splitlines()
        path=request_path_from_changes(changes)
        if not path: return {"ignored":True,"reason":"non_request_or_extra_files"}
        raw=git(env,"-C",str(work),"show","refs/bridge/head:"+path).stdout.encode()
        return {"path":path,"raw":raw}
    except (OSError,subprocess.SubprocessError) as exc: raise Reject('request_git_unavailable') from exc
    finally:
        __import__('shutil').rmtree(work)

def process(number, head, ledger_root, key_path, reader=read_pr):
    ledger=Ledger(ledger_root); key="%s:%s" % (number,head)
    tx=ledger.transaction(); data=next(tx)
    try:
        if key in data["requests"]:
            record=data["requests"][key]
            if record.get("status") == "claiming": raise Reject("ambiguous_claim_requires_operator_review")
            return {"status":"already_seen","record":record}
        proposal=reader(number,head)
        if proposal.get("ignored"):
            data["requests"][key]={"status":"ignored","reason":proposal["reason"]}; return {"status":"ignored"}
        if not REQUEST_RE.fullmatch(proposal["path"]): raise Reject("request_path")
        request=validate_request(proposal["raw"])
        if request['action_id']!=POLICY['action_id']: raise Reject('legacy_mode_verify_only')
        for record in data["requests"].values():
            if record.get("request_id")==request["request_id"]: raise Reject("duplicate_request_id")
        data["requests"][key]={"status":"claiming","request_id":request["request_id"]}
        temp=ledger.root/"ledger.tmp"; temp.write_bytes(canonical(data)); os.chmod(temp,0o600); os.replace(temp,ledger.path)
        preview=sign(derive(request,{"image_id":"sha256:"+"0"*64}),key_path)
        data["requests"][key]={"status":"dry_run_consumed","request_id":request["request_id"],"task_id":preview["task_id"],"task_sha256":__import__("hashlib").sha256(canonical(preview)).hexdigest(),"publish_enabled":False}
        return {"status":"dry_run_consumed","task_id":preview["task_id"],"publish_enabled":False}
    finally:
        try: next(tx)
        except StopIteration: pass

def load_arm(path):
    value=json.loads(pathlib.Path(path).read_text())
    required={"version","state","expected_request_id","max_formal_task_issuances","publish_enabled"}
    if set(value) != required or value["version"] != 1 or value["max_formal_task_issuances"] != 1: raise Reject("invalid_arm_configuration")
    if value["state"] not in {"ARMED","DISARMED_CONSUMED"} or not REQUEST_ID_RE.fullmatch(value["expected_request_id"]): raise Reject("invalid_arm_configuration")
    if not isinstance(value["publish_enabled"],bool): raise Reject("invalid_arm_configuration")
    return value
def save_arm(path, value):
    target=pathlib.Path(path); temporary=target.with_suffix(".tmp"); temporary.write_bytes(canonical(value)); os.chmod(temporary,0o600); os.replace(temporary,target)
def remote_task(task_id):
    work=pathlib.Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="go-boss-reconcile-")); env=ssh_env()
    try:
        git(env,"init","-q",str(work)); git(env,"-C",str(work),"remote","add","origin",REPO); git(env,"-C",str(work),"fetch","-q","--depth","1","origin","main")
        got=subprocess.run(["/usr/bin/git","-C",str(work),"show","FETCH_HEAD:tasks/"+task_id+".json"],env=env,stdout=subprocess.PIPE,stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL)
        return got.stdout if got.returncode == 0 else None
